        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(googlechat): cap two warn-once Sets via createDedupeCache",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes unbounded memory growth in two Google Chat warn-once deduplication Sets. Both `warnedDeprecatedUsersEmailAllowFrom` and `warnedMutableGroupKeys` accumulated every warned key forever with no eviction, TTL, or size cap.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced both unbounded `Set<string>` instances with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`, imported from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/dedupe-runtime` per extension boundary policy. The `check()` method provides touch-on-read LRU semantics.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo change for gateways handling fewer than 4 096 distinct warned keys per cache.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real-path proof — existing tests exercise the warning path in the real module\n\nThe existing 13 `monitor-access.test.ts` tests pass with the patched module. The `\"does not match group policy by mutable space displayName\"` test triggers the `warnMutableGroupKeysConfigured` path, and the verbose log output shows `deprecated mutable group key detected` only once per distinct key — the `warnedMutableGroupKeys.check()` deduplication is exercised through the real runtime path:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm vitest run extensions/googlechat/src/monitor-access.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n ✓ googlechat inbound access policy > does not match group policy by mutable space displayName...\n ... 13 passed (13)\n```\n\n### Cache cap and LRU eviction\n\n`createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` is the same helper used by Telegram and Slack. Cache cap and LRU behavior are verified by unit tests:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm vitest run src/infra/dedupe.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n ✓ createDedupeCache > keeps entries indefinitely when ttlMs is zero or negative\n ✓ createDedupeCache > touches duplicate reads so the newest key survives max-size pruning\n ... 5 passed (5)\n```\n\n### Plugin boundary contract passes\n\n```text\n$ pnpm vitest run src/plugins/contracts/plugin-sdk-package-contract-guardrails.test.ts\n\n ✓ keeps extension sources on public sdk or local package seams  ... 22 passed (22)\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
